-- title:
--   Crossing points on the special fibre of X₀(M'q) are supersingular
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and an integer $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $K_0$ be the intermediate field of $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ generated by the ratios $\mathsf{intSeriesC}(p_f)/\mathsf{intSeriesC}(p_g)$ of integral $\mathsf q$-expansions of modular forms for $\Gamma_0(M'q)$; that is, $K_0$ is generated over $L$ by the image of that field under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}(\!(\mathsf q)\!) \to L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, with $q$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\mathfrak{m}_A = (\varpi)$, and suppose $K_0$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K_0$. Let $j \in K_0$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of $\mathsf{jq} = \mathsf q^{-1}\cdot \mathsf{jNumQ}$, and write $B = \mathsf{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_0\,j$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K_0$ integral over $A[j]$, with $\mathsf{jChartFin}$ the element $j$ of $B$. Let $y \subset B$ be a prime ideal containing $\varpi$ and containing two distinct minimal primes of $\varpi B$. Then for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ (with decidable equality) and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : B \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathsf{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$: every elliptic Weierstrass curve $W$ over $\Omega$ with $W.j = \varphi(j)$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$.
--
--   This is the assertion that the two irreducible components of the special fibre at $q$ of the integral model of $X_0(M'q)$ meet only above supersingular $j$-invariants, phrased on the finite chart (the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K_0$) of the normalisation of the projective $j$-line over an arbitrary discrete valuation ring $A$ of residue characteristic $q$ with fraction field of characteristic zero, and with supersingularity expressed as vanishing of $q$-torsion. It is used in the study of ramification of the chart ring of $\Gamma_0(M'q)$ at primes of the special fibre and in the comparison of Gauss-type maps away from supersingular points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgFin_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_mul.lean

